WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:02.640
Have you ever wondered

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:06.560
if there are more natural ways
to lower your high blood pressure,

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.520
guard against Alzheimer's,
lose weight, and feel better?

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:12.720
Well, it turns out there is!

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:15.200
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.760
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:21.200
Today we wrap up our
series on the enzyme NAD+

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:26.160
and we start with a cautionary tale
about NAD-boosting supplements.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:27.760
Most of the reported
side effects

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:32.160
for NAD+ precursors,
like NAM, NR, and NMN,

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.080
are relatively rare and minor,

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:36.880
for example, diarrhea,
nausea, rashes, hot flashes,

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:38.240
and leg cramps.

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:41.920
Both NR and NMN
raise NAM levels,

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:44.640
so may share
in the same concerns

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:48.240
regarding sirtuin inhibition,
methyl depletion,

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:52.720
and potential adverse effects
of NAM breakdown products.

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:55.600
Another theoretical concern
of NAD+ boosting

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:57.440
is the exacerbation
of infections

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:59.920
by a group of bacteria
called Haemophilus

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:02.320
(from the Greek
meaning "blood loving,"

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:04.640
though can also cause
infections of the lungs,

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:07.280
brain, throat,
flesh, and joints).

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:10.800
Haemophilus bacteria lack
the ability to make NAD+,

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:12.720
so rely on host levels,

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:15.040
raising the possibility
that higher blood levels

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:18.720
might worsen the disease course
of infected individuals.

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:21.040
Ironically,
elevated NAD+ levels

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:24.000
may also fuel
immune system overreaction

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:27.600
in cases of auto-immune
and inflammatory disease.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:31.040
When fully activated,
the immune system is voracious.

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:32.960
The immune reaction
to a blood infection

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:37.120
or extensive burns can burn
4,000 calories a day,

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:40.160
approximating military training
in the Arctic.

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:42.880
Since NAD+ is used by cells
to produce energy,

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:44.320
it's no surprise that we find

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:47.360
the primary NAD+
synthesizing enzyme

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:48.880
strongly upregulated

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:51.280
in tissues
that are actively inflamed.

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:54.960
For example,
the enzyme NAMPT is elevated

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:58.400
in colonoscopy biopsies
taken from inflamed areas

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:01.280
in patients with
inflammatory bowel disease,

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:03.520
and higher levels
are correlated

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:05.840
with greater disease severity.

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:09.360
So, for those suffering from
chronic autoimmune diseases,

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:11.440
such as rheumatoid arthritis,

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:13.520
NAD+ boosting
could potentially have

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:16.080
a "profound negative impact."

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:19.040
This explains
why tamping down NAD+

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:22.240
with NAMPT inhibitors
has been shown

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:25.760
to ameliorate colitis
and arthritis in mice,

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:28.400
but this has yet
to be tested in people.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:31.120
Such NAD+ depleting drugs
have, however,

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:33.840
been used in cancer patients.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:37.920
Malignancy is another heavily
energy-consuming process.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:41.120
NAD+ may, therefore,
have a tumor-promoting effect

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:43.600
by promoting cancer cell growth
and spread.

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:47.120
For example, NAMPT,
the NAD+-forming enzyme,

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:49.520
is highly expressed
in cancerous brain tumors

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:53.040
and correlates with
decreased patient survival.

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:56.320
This has led to attempts
to use NAD+-depleting therapies

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:59.520
to try to starve
cancer progression,

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:02.400
but this approach is confounded
by rapid onset injury

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.640
to another
energy-intensive tissue,

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:08.800
the retina,
risking blindness.

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:11.680
Giving NMN to mice
with pancreatic cancer

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:14.240
accelerates the progression
of the cancer,

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:17.040
thought due to the aggravation
of inflammation.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:20.320
The researchers conclude that
consumers of NAD+ supplements

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:23.360
must "balance the advantageous
anti-ageing effects

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:28.000
with the potential detrimental
pro-tumorigenic side effects."

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:30.800
Perhaps this explains
why the best NAD+ boosters

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:32.160
have ever been able to do

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:35.840
is increase mice lifespan
by five percent.

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:37.440
On the other hand,
as you'll remember,

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:41.040
NAM successfully prevented
human skin cancers

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:43.200
and has been found
to reduce the incidence

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:45.760
of a variety
of carcinogen-induced tumors

00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:46.880
in rodents.

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:49.360
The disparate results
may in part be due

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:51.920
to the disparate impact
sirtuin activation

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:53.680
may have on different cancers.

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:55.680
Sirtuin activity
can be overexpressed

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:56.960
in some cancers

00:03:56.960 --> 00:04:00.000
(like thyroid carcinomas
and lung metastasis)

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.280
but reduced in others

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:03.840
(like brain, bladder, prostate,
and ovarian tumors).

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:07.120
The bottom line
is that particular caution

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:09.600
should be used
for NAD+-boosting supplements

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:11.040
by those with cancer,

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:13.920
or a personal or strong
family history of cancer,

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:16.800
and perhaps also by those
with inflammatory disorders

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:19.600
and certain active infections.

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:20.480
In our next story,

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:24.800
we look at how to naturally get
our bodies to make more NAD+

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:29.920
by boosting the NAD+-synthesizing
enzyme NAMPT.

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:33.520
So, which NAD+ boosting
supplement is best?

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:35.120
There’s no clear standout,

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:38.080
as hardly any of the preclinical
effects found in the lab

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:41.600
have translated into evidence
of human clinical benefit.

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:46.960
Perhaps, this failure is to be expected
given the complexity of NAD+ physiology,

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:52.240
with its juggling of multiple precursors,
production pathways, and recycling routes.

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:56.560
The bottom line is that it’s just too early
to say if NAD+ booster supplementation

00:04:56.560 --> 00:05:00.080
will ever live up to even
a fraction of the hype.

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:05.520
Many more, larger, and longer-term studies
are necessary to establish safety and efficacy.

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:11.680
The problem is that because NA, NAM,
NR, and NMN are all natural products,

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:13.200
they can’t be patented;

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:17.440
so, the money for well-designed
clinical trials is not as available.

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:21.760
The reason there have been comparatively
more trials done on NR than NMN

00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:28.960
is that patents were originally issued for NR
before being invalidated as unpatentable.

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:33.120
Perhaps blindly overloading the
system with NAD+ precursors

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:36.640
is not the best way to go
about NAD+ restoration.

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:43.040
The body seems too smart to allow such
blunt incursion to affect tissue levels.

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:46.000
Maybe these supplements are
just profit-making distractions

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:49.280
from more natural approaches.

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:54.480
Broadly, there are three main
ways to increase NAD+ levels.

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:58.480
Increasing the supply of NAD+
precursors is just the first.

00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:01.440
The other two are having
the body make more,

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:04.000
by activating NAD+
synthesizing enzymes,

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:10.480
or have the body use less, via an
inhibition of excess NAD+ degradation.

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:16.800
The primary determinant of NAD+
synthesis in the enzyme NAMPT.

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:21.280
An abundance of NAMPT tends to
decrease with age in human muscle,

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:25.200
dropping steadily by about 40%
between the ages of 20 and 80.

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:27.600
In our liver, it drops by half.

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:30.880
However, age-related diseases,
such as atherosclerosis,

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:32.720
cancer, diabetes,
and rheumatoid arthritis,

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:36.400
have been found to exacerbate
NAMPT decline,

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:38.880
raising a chicken or
the egg question.

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:42.240
There’s where interventional
trials come in.

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:46.960
Similar NAMPT declines have been
noted in aging rats and mice.

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:49.680
Does boosting NAMPT help?

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:53.920
Increasing NAMPT or its species
equivalent increases the lifespans

00:06:53.920 --> 00:06:56.560
of yeast, fruit flies, and rodents.

00:06:56.560 --> 00:07:02.320
An NAMPT boost also increases aerobic
capacity and exercise endurance in mice,

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:05.280
in addition to helping them live longer.

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:10.080
Enhanced expression of NAMPT increases
the NAD+ levels in the muscles in mice

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:14.320
comparable to feeding them
dietary NAD+ precursors,

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:15.040
but if you remember,

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:20.160
NAD+ precursors don’t seem to be able to
affect NAD+ muscle levels in most people.

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:23.680
In fact, such supplements can
actually suppress NAMPT,

00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:28.160
while boosting that methylating enzyme
to rid the body of the excess.

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:30.080
In addition to methyl depletion,

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:31.920
chronic administration
of these supplements

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:36.080
could potentially then leave people
worse off should they ever stop them.

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:40.960
There is, however, a way to naturally
boost NAMPT and NAD+ levels in humans

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:43.200
without any supplements: exercise.

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:47.120
Athletes have about twice the NAMPT
expression in their musculature

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:49.440
compared to sedentary individuals.

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:51.280
To prove cause and effect,

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:55.920
sedentary men and women started
a stationary bike exercise protocol,

00:07:55.920 --> 00:08:01.360
and within three weeks, NAMPT
levels increased by 127%.

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:04.880
Resistance training can
also increase NAMPT,

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:09.760
and this can also translate into a
127% increase in muscle NAD+ levels

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:12.640
and a rise in sirtuin activity.

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:13.600
In other words,

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:18.560
exercise can do what NAD+
boosting supplements can’t.

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:20.240
Finally today,

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:25.280
how can we conserve NAD+
by preventing over-activation

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:33.200
of the enzymes PARP-1 and CD38,
which both guzzle down NAD+?

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:36.240
There are three
NAD+ boosting strategies:

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:39.040
Increasing the supply
of NAD+ precursors

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:40.320
is just one way.

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:42.880
The other two
are having the body make more,

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:45.360
by activating
NAD+-synthesizing enzymes,

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:49.040
or have the body use less,
by, for example,

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:51.360
conserving it, by using less.

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:53.920
Besides sirtuins,
the major consumers

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:57.760
of NAD+ are PARP-1 and CD38.

00:08:57.760 --> 00:09:02.800
PARP-1 is an enzyme
that uses NAD+ to repair DNA.

00:09:02.800 --> 00:09:04.880
The more oxidative DNA damage,

00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:08.240
the more single
and double stranded DNA breaks,

00:09:08.240 --> 00:09:10.960
the more enzymes like PARP-1
need to be activated

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:12.800
to come to the rescue.

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:16.000
This uses up a lot of NAD.

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:18.320
As DNA damage
accumulates with age,

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:20.960
the rising need
for repair enzymes like PARP-1

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:24.560
causes a major drain
on NAD+ levels.

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:27.600
Exposing cells in vitro
to DNA damaging agents,

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:30.880
such as gamma radiation
or genotoxic chemicals,

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:33.200
can cause an 80
to 90 percent drop

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:36.240
in NAD+ levels
within a matter of minutes.

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:38.640
This has led to the search
for PARP-1 blockers

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:40.960
to preserve NAD+ levels,

00:09:40.960 --> 00:09:43.760
but rather than blocking
DNA repair,

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:45.920
why not work to prevent
so much damage

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:47.440
in the first place?

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:49.360
For example,
the severe oxidative stress

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:50.880
of a high-fat diet

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:54.960
can lead to PARP-1 activation
and NAD+ depletion in mice,

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:57.840
but NAD+ levels can be
"dramatically restored"

00:09:57.840 --> 00:10:00.560
by feeding them
"purple sweet potato color,"

00:10:00.560 --> 00:10:02.800
the natural
anthocyanin pigments

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:05.120
found in purple sweet potatoes.

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:09.760
Or, of course, you can just not
feed them a high-fat diet.

00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:12.800
DNA repair is a good thing.

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:14.320
PARP-1 may be
one of the reasons

00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:17.120
NAD+-boosting interventions
can improve healthspans

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:19.520
and lifespans
in laboratory animals.

00:10:19.520 --> 00:10:22.080
Greater PARP activity
strongly correlates

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:23.600
with longer lifespan

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:25.760
across about a dozen
mammalian species,

00:10:25.760 --> 00:10:28.080
and the PARP activity
of human centenarians

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:31.600
averages 60 percent higher
than younger controls.

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:35.840
However, persistent activation
can lead to NAD+ depletion,

00:10:35.840 --> 00:10:38.560
and overactivation
can lead to cell death.

00:10:38.560 --> 00:10:41.920
So, we should try to keep
oxidative stress to a minimum.

00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:47.440
CD38 is another major guzzler
of NAD+.

00:10:47.440 --> 00:10:49.360
It's an enzyme that uses NAD+

00:10:49.360 --> 00:10:51.360
found concentrated
on the surfaces

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:53.760
of immune cells
and robustly induced

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:56.960
in the context of inflammation.

00:10:56.960 --> 00:10:59.680
The rise of CD38 activity
with age

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:03.120
has been blamed on persistent
"inflammaging" activation,

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:06.960
the rise in systemic low-grade
inflammation in our bodies

00:11:06.960 --> 00:11:07.920
when we get older,

00:11:07.920 --> 00:11:11.760
which may be a major culprit
for falling NAD+ levels.

00:11:11.760 --> 00:11:14.320
For example, blocking CD38
has been found

00:11:14.320 --> 00:11:16.560
to raise NAD+ levels
in old mice

00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:19.120
comparable to that
of younger mice.

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:23.040
So, oxidation and inflammation

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:25.520
can lead to a drop
in NAD+ levels,

00:11:25.520 --> 00:11:30.240
due to the excess activation
of the NAD+ consuming enzymes.

00:11:30.240 --> 00:11:32.880
This may explain why
protective sirtuin activity

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:35.840
is reduced in obesity,
a condition characterized

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:38.480
by oxidative stress
and inflammation.

00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:40.800
A study of identical twin pairs

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:44.480
in which one, on average,
was obese and the other not,

00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:47.280
found significantly
less sirtuin expression

00:11:47.280 --> 00:11:48.960
in the obese twin,

00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:51.360
despite having
the same genetics.

00:11:51.360 --> 00:11:53.360
And randomize people
to a six-month trial

00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:55.680
of 25 percent
calorie restriction,

00:11:55.680 --> 00:11:57.920
and you can show a boost
in sirtuin expression

00:11:57.920 --> 00:12:01.520
along with a decrease
in DNA damage.

00:12:01.520 --> 00:12:03.680
Protein restriction
may have a similar effect,

00:12:03.680 --> 00:12:05.760
since men and women
with higher protein intake

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:08.800
tend to have lower levels
of NAD+ in their blood,

00:12:08.800 --> 00:12:10.880
thought to be due
to the oxidative stress

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:14.000
induced by protein
breakdown byproducts.

00:12:14.560 --> 00:12:17.120
If oxidation and inflammation
are responsible

00:12:17.120 --> 00:12:18.960
for a drop in NAD+ levels,

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:20.960
then what about the antioxidant

00:12:20.960 --> 00:12:23.200
and anti-inflammatory
phytonutrients

00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:25.120
in healthy plant foods?

00:12:25.120 --> 00:12:28.080
After screening
more than 14,000 compounds,

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:30.720
almost all flavonoids
were found to be effective

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:33.280
in a test for CD38 inhibition.

00:12:33.280 --> 00:12:36.160
The two most effective
were cyanidin,

00:12:36.160 --> 00:12:38.480
found in red cabbage
and blackberries,

00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:42.880
and quercetagetin,
found in marigold flower tea.

00:12:42.880 --> 00:12:45.280
Another study found
the three most potent compounds

00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:49.840
were luteolin, kuromanin,
and luteolinidin.

00:12:49.840 --> 00:12:53.680
Luteolin is found concentrated
in oregano, radicchio,

00:12:53.680 --> 00:12:56.160
and chrysanthemum tea.

00:12:56.160 --> 00:12:59.120
Kuromanin is found
in black berries, purple corn,

00:12:59.120 --> 00:13:00.800
and hibiscus tea.

00:13:00.800 --> 00:13:03.280
Corn tortillas are
surprisingly easy to make;

00:13:03.280 --> 00:13:06.000
so why not choose blue
or purple masa

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:07.920
to make them even healthier?

00:13:07.920 --> 00:13:09.120
Luteolinidin,

00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:11.440
found to increase NAD+
in the hearts of rats,

00:13:11.440 --> 00:13:13.680
can be found in red sorghum,

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:16.320
one of the components
of my prebiotic BROL mix,

00:13:16.320 --> 00:13:18.160
when I can find it.

00:13:18.160 --> 00:13:19.680
The flavonoid apigenin

00:13:19.680 --> 00:13:22.480
is a well-established
CD38 inhibitor.

00:13:22.480 --> 00:13:26.080
When given to mice,
apigenin boosts NAD+ levels

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:29.120
by about 50 percent,
which is what people would get

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:32.960
taking the maximum
tolerable daily dose of NR.

00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:36.800
The best sources are parsley
and chamomile tea.

00:13:37.440 --> 00:13:40.400
A wide range of flavonoids
found in green tea, turmeric,

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:42.400
and fruits and vegetables
have also been found

00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:45.760
to prevent NAD+ depletion
in human cells in vitro

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:48.640
at levels found in the blood
after consumption.

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:51.680
How much do you have to eat,
though?

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:54.720
Proanthocyanidins have been
found to lower PARP-1

00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:57.920
and CD38 expression in rats.

00:13:57.920 --> 00:14:00.800
NAD+ and sirtuin activity
was significantly boosted

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:05.280
at the human equivalent dose
of about 280 milligrams a day.

00:14:05.280 --> 00:14:06.960
How much is that?

00:14:06.960 --> 00:14:09.120
That's the amount
of proanthocyanidins

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:12.240
found in a single apple.

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:15.760
You could also reach that dose
eating two plums,

00:14:15.760 --> 00:14:17.680
a half cup of wild blueberries,

00:14:17.680 --> 00:14:19.920
a little over a teaspoon
of cinnamon,

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:22.480
or a little over a tablespoon,
like four teaspoons,

00:14:22.480 --> 00:14:23.920
of cocoa powder.

00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:26.880
Quercetin is another suppressor
of PARP-1 and CD38

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:29.760
shown to increase
sirtuin activity in mice.

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:32.880
The concentration necessary
to lower PARP-1 in vitro

00:14:32.880 --> 00:14:35.920
can be achieved by taking
a quercetin supplement,

00:14:35.920 --> 00:14:37.920
but typical supplement
manufacturers'

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:40.560
recommended doses
are up to 100 times

00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:42.880
the average daily
dietary intake.

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:46.080
Thankfully, food works too.

00:14:46.080 --> 00:14:48.480
Researchers fried up
one and a half yellow onions

00:14:48.480 --> 00:14:50.000
and raised
quercetin blood levels

00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:52.320
to about 75 percent there.

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:55.040
And so, two onions might do it.

00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:56.960
There's no long-term
safety data

00:14:56.960 --> 00:14:59.200
on high-dose
flavonoid supplementation;

00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:01.360
so, public health researchers
suggest

00:15:01.360 --> 00:15:04.240
"caution should be exercised
in ingesting them

00:15:04.240 --> 00:15:06.720
at levels above which
would be obtained

00:15:06.720 --> 00:15:11.520
from a typical
vegetarian diet."

